but he wants her to be able to be  herself and make her own decisions  annie has lived her entire life obeying  the orders of others  even when she herself didn't believe in  those orders  so now she should finally get the chance  to follow her  own path i have to say that i'm pretty  surprised to see annie staying out of  the fight  after finally emerging from the crystal  after all those years  but who knows maybe this is just a psych  out by isayama and annie will end up  getting drawn into the fight eventually  only time will tell then in a weird but  kind of classic hanji moment she asks  pique to let her ride  on the back of her titan and peek is  like uh  no dude what's with your creepy titan  fetish  and levi then teases hanji about yet  another titan  failing to return her love hanji  proceeds to ask levi  a very poignant question she asks him if  he thinks that all their dead comrades  are watching them  and she asks if they will be able to  stand tall among their dead comrades  when the time comes levi tells hanji not  to start talking like  him referring of course to the one and  only captain erwin  but just as the allies make all the  necessary preparations  and just as the airplane is almost ready  for takeoff freaking flock  shows up yet again he didn't die back on  parodies  just as i suspected since we never  actually saw his body  and it turns out that he had somehow  held onto the ship  all the way to odiha despite being  injured flock manages to crawl his way  inside the airplane hangar and he uses  his gun to shoot up the airplane and of  course he does this in an attempt to  stop the plane from being able to take  off as everyone scrambles to dodge the  bullets  mikasa uses the steel hook on her  vertical maneuvering gear to pierce  flock's throat as flock lays there dying  oyan component the engineers realized  that he has managed to shoot holes  through the airplane's fuel tank just  when the plane was finally prepared to  take off  it now has holes in the fuel tank which  means that it won't be able to take off  after all  not unless it is fixed immediately the  engineers will need an hour to weld  the holes shut but that's more time than  they actually have  because in that very moment the tools on  the table begin to rattle  it is as if an earthquake is hitting the  hangar but in reality  it is the rumbling the titans are  almost here as the rumbling descends  upon odiha  the engineers struggle to fix the  airplane and to get it  airborne with his final breath flock  warns his comrades yet again  that stopping aaron would bring about  the end of everyone on parodies  their devil aaron is their  only hope i didn't think about this  while writing the script but now that  i'm recording i remember that i made an  entire video  talking about how aaron might actually  be the earth devil  that historia learned about in the story  books about emir fritz  now that we know everything about  aaron's future memories and how he  entices emir fritz to join him and  create this entire rumbling  that theory is starting to make even  more sense  to be fair it wasn't the earth devil who  initially gave emir fritz the titan  powers  as we originally thought but it was  aaron who enticed emir fritz  to launch the rumbling along with him  anyway  in that moment the divine king emperor  flock forster  dies clearly this is the single most  tragic death in all of attack on titan  so far now you know what i meant  in the introduction of the video i mean  it's hard to even talk right now i need  some time to grieve  please everyone f's in the chat for our  boy  flock he will definitely be missed by  someone  i guess hanji is well aware that flock  has a point  and she knows that some sort of real  lasting peace between the nations  seems impossible right now and that is  of course why aaron decided to do what  he is doing now  but hanji still has hope that one day  things could change  she refuses to give up and she refuses  to stand by as aaron destroys the entire  world  upon realizing that the titans are  almost there gabby and falco  tried to escape their room and help but  annie refuses to let them out  and kilmi shovels coal into the ship's  engine  in order to get it moving annie carries  out her duty  and protects gabby and falco as promised  and the steam ship successfully departs  and leaves odiha behind back on land  the allies know that they don't have  enough time to get the plane airborned  before the titans arrive  someone will need to stay behind and  slow the titans down  at the cost of their own life armin  volunteers to do it  since being suicidal is kind of his  thing now and then reiner volunteers  saying that they need armin in order to  stop aaron but in the end  hanji decides that she will be the one  to make the ultimate sacrifice  they can't afford to lose anyone who is  a shifter their powers are too valuable  so hanji promotes armin to the 15th  commander of the survey corps and  she takes the responsibility for slowing  down the titans  upon herself i find it kind of crazy  that hanji says that there is no one  more suited for the duty of being  commander than armin  especially with how armin has been  acting lately like did we forget that he  almost  fed himself to connie's mother just a  few chapters ago  but hey he's a good strategist so i  guess that's why he's indispensable  whatever  let's just go with it hanji then says  goodbye to everyone and as she walks  away she comes  face to face with levi hanji tells levi  to let her go  since it's finally her turn to make the  ultimate sacrifice  and she wants to look as cool as  possible as she does this  one final act unclearly emotional levi  grabs hanji's caller and says  sageo and hanji actually laughs because  she never heard him say those words  before  man this was truly an emotional moment  especially when we think back to that  time that levi and hanji spent in the  woods  back then as hanji was nursing levi back  to health after zeke's explosion  for a moment she considered just staying  alone in the woods with levi forever  but of course she couldn't do that they  couldn't just sit by and do nothing as  the entire world burned  and now they must face the consequences  of that  choice the chapter ends with hanji  zooming off to face the colossal titans  head on  and even as she prepares to engage in  the final battle of her life  hanji can't help but admire the wall  titans in all of their grotesque  glory hanji stays true to herself and  her quirky personality  until the very end she bravely takes  down  several titans who had been closest to  the city and this buys the allies just  enough time to fix the plane  and take off in the last possible moment  the wall titans are so hot that just  being close to them  is making hanji's clothes and entire  body catch on fire but  even so she continues to fight on  fiercely she keeps attacking and slicing  at the nape of the titans  even as her own body literally burns  and then as both the ship and the  airplane take off  in the nick of time hanji's body is  consumed by flames  and eventually it is crushed beneath the  feet of the titans  oh obviously this is a really sad and  emotional moment for all of us  long time fans of attack on titan hanji  has been such a pivotal character  and an extremely likable character for  most of the story she was funny  smart a little crazy and she played a  key role in keeping the scouts together  through all the pain and suffering that  they went through after the death of  irwin but here's the interesting  thing unlike the vast majority of deaths  in attack on titan  hanji's death is not portrayed in a  graphically violent or gruesome way  we see her corpse only from a bird's eye  view and from a great distance  and then we see her wake up her body  fully  intact she is suddenly surrounded by all  her former comrades from the survey  corps who lost their lives in the past  including erwin  sasha shadis and more as the airplane  flies away  the survey corps members help hanji to  her feet  and she immediately begins to complain  to irwin about all the trouble he caused  her by naming her commander  and she also complains about aaron being  an idiot and  that is where this tragic and yet  powerful chapter  ends the final images that we see of  hanji  are not images of her brutally mutilated  corpse they are  images of her joining her comrades in  the afterlife  and she looks normal as if she never  even went through that final battle  against the titans whether you think  that this afterlife is just symbolic or  whether you believe that it is real  i think that hanji's death shows just  how much isayama respected her character  he wanted us to remember hanji the way  that she was in life  and he wanted us to think of her as a  faithful survey corps member who did her  duty  and then joined her comrades in a  peaceful afterlife  isa emma could easily have made it so  that the last time we saw hanji she was  just a charred  and flattened corpse and certainly in  attack on titan  seeing such gruesome images is nothing  new but  islama didn't do that and i believe that  this was very much  intentional he wanted to pay a special  kind of respect  to this memorable and beloved character  and i think he succeeded  as attack on titan fans we are almost  desensitized to the gory graphic and  brutal deaths of the past  so the fact that hanji's death was  portrayed differently makes it more  memorable  hanji's death was of course tragic but  it was also powerful  and even beautiful in its own way  despite all the death that we have  witnessed in attack on titan  you can never really get used to such an  important character dying  but i think that in this moment we can  all come together to honor  hanji's life courage and sacrifice  and after we pay our respects we have to  ask ourselves  what happens next the allies now have a  rough idea  of where aar